0025: def main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:
0026:     """
0027:     Recolor the concentric rectangular rings by cycling the outside-to-inside color order one step outward.
0028: 
0029:     Input structure:
0030:     - The whole grid is partitioned into one-cell-thick concentric rectangular rings.
0031:     - Each ring is monochromatic.
0032:     - Reading rings from outside to inside gives at least two distinct colors; a color may reappear on a later ring.
0033: 
0034:     Rule:
0035:     - Record the distinct colors in their first outside-to-inside ring order.
0036:     - Replace every pixel of each recorded color with the previous color in that cyclic order.
0037: 
0038:     Key insight:
0039:     - The transformation is a color-cycle over nesting order, not over numeric color ids or ring sizes.
0040:     """
